# 2. RATIO & PROPORTION

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## CORE IDEA

Ratio:

```
a : b
```

means:

```
a/b
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## PATTERN A — DIVIDE TOTAL IN RATIO

Total:

```
T
```

Ratio:

```
a:b
```

Total parts:

```
a+b
```

One part:

```
T/(a+b)
```

Therefore:

```
First = T × a/(a+b)

Second = T × b/(a+b)
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## PATTERN B — RATIO CHANGE

If:

```
A:B = 2:3
```

and total:

```
50
```

Then:

```
A = 20
B = 30
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## PATTERN C — PROPORTION

```
a:b = c:d
```

means:

```
a/b = c/d
```

Therefore:

```
ad = bc
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## PATTERN D — DIRECT PROPORTION

If:

```
more A → more B
```

then:

```
A ∝ B
```

Example:

```
More workers
→ more output
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## INVERSE PROPORTION

If:

```
more A → less B
```

then:

```
A ∝ 1/B
```

Example:

```
More workers
→ less time
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
ratio
divided in
proportion
share
workers and time
boys and girls

    ↓

RATIO
```

