# 3. PROFIT / LOSS / DISCOUNT

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## CORE VARIABLES

```
CP = Cost Price
SP = Selling Price
MP = Marked Price
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## PROFIT

```
Profit = SP - CP
```

Profit %:

```
Profit/CP × 100
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## LOSS

```
Loss = CP - SP
```

Loss %:

```
Loss/CP × 100
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## PROFIT FORMULA

If profit = p%:

```
SP =
CP × (100+p)/100
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## LOSS FORMULA

If loss = l%:

```
SP =
CP × (100-l)/100
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## DISCOUNT

```
Discount = MP - SP
```

Discount %:

```
Discount/MP × 100
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## SUCCESSIVE DISCOUNTS

Discounts:

```
a%
b%
```

Net discount:

```
a + b - ab/100
```

Example:

```
20%, 10%

= 20 + 10 - 2
= 28%
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
bought
sold
cost
selling
marked
discount
profit
loss

    ↓

PROFIT / LOSS
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## TRAP

Profit % is calculated on:

```
COST PRICE
```

Discount % is calculated on:

```
MARKED PRICE
```

