# 5. TIME & WORK

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## CORE IDEA

If A completes work in:

```
x days
```

A's one-day work:

```
1/x
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## TWO PEOPLE

A:

```
1/x
```

B:

```
1/y
```

Together:

```
1/x + 1/y
```

Time:

```
1 /
(1/x + 1/y)
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## FAST METHOD

A takes:

```
x days
```

B takes:

```
y days
```

Together:

```
xy/(x+y)
```

Example:

```
A = 10 days
B = 15 days
```

Together:

```
10×15/(10+15)

= 150/25

= 6 days
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## WORKER-DAY METHOD

If:

```
10 workers
× 6 days
```

Total work:

```
60 worker-days
```

Therefore:

```
workers × days = constant
```

when efficiency is same.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## EFFICIENCY

If:

```
A is 2× as efficient as B
```

Then:

```
A's time = half B's time.
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
complete work
finish work
workers
days
efficiency
alone
together

    ↓

TIME & WORK
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## MASTER STORY

```
TIME
  ↓
RATE
  ↓
WORK

Work = Rate × Time
```

