# 7. MIXTURE & ALLEGATION

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## CORE IDEA

When two quantities with different prices/concentrations
are mixed to obtain a mean value:

```
    CHEAPER
       │
       │
    MEAN
       │
       │
    DEARER
```

Ratio:

```
CHEAPER : DEARER

    =
(DEARER - MEAN)
:
(MEAN - CHEAPER)
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## EXAMPLE

₹20 mixture

and

₹50 mixture

want:

₹30 mixture

Ratio:

```
cheaper : dearer

= (50-30):(30-20)

= 20:10

= 2:1
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CONCENTRATION

Same concept:

```
water
+ milk

acid
+ water

alcohol
+ water
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
mixture
concentration
alloy
milk/water
price per kg
average price

    ↓

ALLEGATION
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## MASTER MEMORY

```
DIFFERENCE FROM MEAN

    opposite side's difference

    ↓

RATIO
```

