# 15. PERMUTATION & COMBINATION

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## PERMUTATION

ORDER MATTERS.

```
nPr =
n!/(n-r)!
```

Example:

```
arrange people
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## COMBINATION

ORDER DOES NOT MATTER.

```
nCr =
n!/[r!(n-r)!]
```

Example:

```
select committee
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## MEMORY

```
ARRANGE
   ↓
PERMUTATION


SELECT
   ↓
COMBINATION
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## IMPORTANT RELATION

```
nCr = nC(n-r)
```

Use the smaller r.

